  "question": {
    "text": "The quantity of electricity in Faraday needed to reduce <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>1 faraday of charge is the magnitude of charge of one mole of electrons.</p><p>According to the given reaction:&nbsp;<br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#10230;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />Reduction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></math> of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> to <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;requires&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> moles of electrons. Hence, charge required <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Faraday</mi></math></p>"
  }
